Input: {"question": "What is the mascot of West Valley High School?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0421-f776194ffec1:d00", "start": 0, "end": 255, "text": "West Valley High School (Cottonwood, California) West Valley High School is an American high school located at 3805 Happy Valley Road, Cottonwood, California, 96022, 6.5 miles west of Interstate 5 near the intersection of Gas Point and Happy Valley Roads."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0421-f776194ffec1:d00", "start": 256, "end": 351, "text": "The closest major city is Redding, California which is about fifteen miles north of the school."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0421-f776194ffec1:d00", "start": 352, "end": 385, "text": "The school's mascot is the eagle."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0421-f776194ffec1:d00", "start": 386, "end": 446, "text": "West Valley is a small school of approximately 900 students."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0421-f776194ffec1:d00", "start": 447, "end": 547, "text": "It is part of the Anderson Union High School District which is headed by superintendent Tim Azevedo."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0421-f776194ffec1:d00", "start": 548, "end": 631, "text": "The district includes Anderson, Anderson New Technology, Oakview, North Valley, and"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0421-f776194ffec1:d01", "start": 0, "end": 160, "text": "West Valley High School (Hemet, California) West Valley High School is a high school that serves around 1,800 students on the western side of Hemet, California."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0421-f776194ffec1:d01", "start": 161, "end": 282, "text": "The school is accredited by the WASC Accrediting Commission for Schools and also has become an AVID Demonstration School."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0421-f776194ffec1:d01", "start": 283, "end": 331, "text": "The West Valley High School mascot is a Mustang."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0421-f776194ffec1:d01", "start": 332, "end": 435, "text": "West Valley High School was created in 1989 to accommodate the growing population of Hemet, California."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0421-f776194ffec1:d01", "start": 436, "end": 585, "text": "The student and teacher population of Hemet Junior High (closed in 1990) worked to create a name, mascot and colors (maroon and gray) for the school."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0421-f776194ffec1:d01", "start": 586, "end": 607, "text": "West Valley opened in"}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0421-f776194ffec1:d02", "start": 0, "end": 122, "text": "West Valley High School (Spokane, Washington) West Valley High School is a public secondary school in Spokane, Washington."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0421-f776194ffec1:d02", "start": 123, "end": 175, "text": "It enrolls over 900 students in grades 9 through 12."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0421-f776194ffec1:d02", "start": 176, "end": 244, "text": "The school colors are orange and black and the mascot is the eagles."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0421-f776194ffec1:d02", "start": 245, "end": 346, "text": "As a Gates \"Washington Achievers\" grant high school, West Valley has started a mentor groups program."}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0421-f776194ffec1:d02", "start": 347, "end": 538, "text": "Staff members meet with small groups of students daily to discuss issues in students' lives and connect with the students in the hopes that it will improve student experience and performance."}, "D3S6": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0421-f776194ffec1:d02", "start": 539, "end": 616, "text": "Student clubs at West Valley High School include band, DECA, Drama, Knowledge"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": 